Upstream attribution (MIT)
--------------------------
Release 4.0.4 re-implements, line by line and with its own tests, the following
changes of Hyundai-Kia-Connect/hyundai_kia_connect_api (MIT License, tag
v5.3.1, commit 750e4e2):

- PR #1416: current browser User-Agent for the EU OneApp signin.
- PR #1352, commit 97668164 (2026-10-14): X-Fingerprint signing of the CCI
  auth calls and gate-only legacy fallback. Kia constants and scheme in
  cci_fingerprint.py; PR #1358 (cci_auth.py refactor) shaped the structure.
- PR #1342: random device identity when the legacy device register fails.
- PR #1477: typed authentication errors (redirect, sign-in, invalid credentials,
  token exchange).
- PR #1536: hint for passwords longer than 20 characters.
- PR #1506 and PR #1507: removal of the 48-character token login and of the
  refresh_token grant.
- PR #1579 (margin part only): CCS token rotation margin of 360 seconds with a
  300 second floor, from issue #1446.

The login limit (login_guard.py) is original to this repository.
